From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: XP's simulated bold in the XP shell's session

Purpose: the XP shell's large bold headings in fonts without a bold face
look as on XP: Control Panel's "Pick a category" (Franklin Gothic Medium
21pt at weight 700, from the Luna shellstyle.dll), the Start panel's user
name and the Welcome screen.
Windows behavior: GDI simulates bold by widening each glyph one pixel to
the right, at every size, and adds that pixel to its advance.
Wine before: the outline was emboldened by ppem/24 in both directions
(FreeType), over a pixel each way at 28 pixels: the heading looked like a
black weight. The advance already got the one pixel.
Change: in the XP shell's session, the outline is widened one pixel
horizontally (FT_Outline_EmboldenXY) and moved half a pixel right, as the
embedded bitmaps already are.
Scope: the XP shell's session (the Windows 7 and ReactOS sessions keep
their measured text); synthetic bold of outline glyphs.
---
 dlls/win32u/freetype.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
index 8e346ac..fb45d3a 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
@@ -114,6 +114,7 @@ MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_MulFix);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_New_Face);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_New_Memory_Face);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Embolden);
+MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_EmboldenXY);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Get_Bitmap);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Get_CBox);
 MAKE_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Transform);
@@ -1490,6 +1491,7 @@ static BOOL init_freetype(void)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_New_Face)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_New_Memory_Face)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Embolden)
+    LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_EmboldenXY)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Get_Bitmap)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Get_CBox)
     LOAD_FUNCPTR(FT_Outline_Transform)
@@ -2379,8 +2381,18 @@ static BOOL get_bold_glyph_outline(FT_GlyphSlot glyph, LONG ppem, FT_Glyph_Metri
     if(glyph->format != FT_GLYPH_FORMAT_OUTLINE)
         return FALSE;
 
-    strength = pFT_MulDiv(ppem, 1 << 6, 24);
-    err = pFT_Outline_Embolden(&glyph->outline, strength);
+    /* XP's simulated bold widens the glyph by one pixel to the right,
+       whatever its size; the advance gets the same pixel. */
+    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_XP)
+    {
+        err = pFT_Outline_EmboldenXY(&glyph->outline, 1 << 6, 0);
+        if (!err) pFT_Outline_Translate(&glyph->outline, 1 << 5, 0);
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        strength = pFT_MulDiv(ppem, 1 << 6, 24);
+        err = pFT_Outline_Embolden(&glyph->outline, strength);
+    }
     if(err) {
         TRACE("FT_Ouline_Embolden returns %d\n", err);
         return FALSE;
